00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
-♪♪ Mad Lib Theater,
ah-ahh, yeah ♪♪

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, here's how it works.
I'm going to ask you...

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:07.007 size:78% position:39%
-Here's how it works.
-...some silly words.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.209
-Pretend you're in the back
of a 1976 station wagon.

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:11.344
-Yes. Exactly like that. And you
get that little flip thing.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:14.014
I'm gonna ask silly words,
nouns, verbs, adjectives.

00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.216
As we do that, they're going to
be written onto cue cards.

00:00:16.216 --> 00:00:17.650
-This is going to be a real test
of my education.

00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:20.620
-And we're going to act out
a dramatic Mad Libs scene.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
All right. Ready for this?
-Yes, sir.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:26.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Here we go. Name of
a famous cartoon character?

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.161 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Popeye.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:30.296 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Type of car?

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:33.066 line:92%
-A Pinto. Pinto. A Pinto.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Pinto, Pinto, Pinto.
Okay, perfect.

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, three or four of 'em.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.538 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
